<%- include('../partials/header') %>
<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-6">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Disclaimer</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">Please read this before using CloakTail.</p>

  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 text-sm leading-relaxed">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">For development and testing only</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        CloakTail and its <code><%= sandboxRealm %></code> sandbox realm are provided to help developers build and test SAML integrations.
        They are not a production identity service. Do not connect production applications to the sandbox or rely on it for real users.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">No real personal data or credentials</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        Test users must use made-up names and email addresses. Never enter real people’s personal data, and never reuse a password you use anywhere else.
        SAML test results, including attribute values and the raw response, are stored in the portal and visible to administrators.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">Generated keys and certificates</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        The certificate generator creates self-signed certificates for sandbox testing. Keys are generated on the portal server, sent to your browser once and not stored,
        but they are not suitable for production. Generate production keys on infrastructure you control and keep private keys secret.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">Availability and data retention</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        The sandbox is provided as-is, without any service level or warranty. Applications, test users and test history may be changed, reset or deleted at any time,
        for example when an account is removed or the sandbox is rebuilt. Keep your own copy of any configuration you need.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        Use the portal only to integrate applications you are authorised to work on. Do not use it to impersonate other services, collect other people’s credentials,
        or probe or overload Keycloak. Activity is logged, and accounts that misuse the portal may be disabled without notice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">Your responsibility</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        A successful test in the sandbox does not guarantee your application is secure or production-ready.
        You remain responsible for your application’s SAML configuration, certificate handling and security review before going live.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
